      "side": 1,
      "message": "GTS does use 429s to provide temporary rate-limiting of individual accounts along with an appropriate Retry-After header for POST requests. I think this conforms to all specs.\n\nWould it be possible to retry the request if a 429 response contained a Retry-After header? Any 429 that didn\u0027t contain the guidance would immediately return?\n\nRoland probably has context on LE\u0027s thoughts here.\nhttps://github.com/letsencrypt/boulder/issues/4104",
      "revId": "c20c136be7c4e5ffdc872abdf3d950ef7345013a",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
    {
