      "writtenOn": "2020-11-25T16:42:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh hm, that is completely reasonable and would be good to support. At LE we never implemented Retry-After for most rate limits because it was incredibly hard to calculate for more complex limits, but it is entirely spec compliant.\n\nGating retrying on 429 on the presence of a Retry-After header seems reasonable (although I guess we could run into the same issue where a server sets a Retry-After that is hours or days in the future... that is fixed by just setting a reasonable context though I guess).",
      "parentUuid": "6c1d079c_37afc578",
